{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/42302-new-player-new-gm-help-with-scion","id":42302,"title":"New Player/New GM help with Scion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-04T08:46:24-08:00","id":42302,"title":"New Player/New GM help with Scion","content":"Hello everyone, I am new to the Scion game. I will be both playing a game and also running one (with different groups). The GM that I am playing with is also brand new to the Scion game, we are both seeking some assistance with the game and would appreciate any help. The first question/conundrum we have is concerning RELICS and CREATURES, FOLLOWERS, GUIDES. For CREATURES, FOLLOWERS, GUIDES we are a little lost on how to actually &quot;create&quot; the stat block for these things, there not too many examples and the examples even seem to vary a bit at the same DOT cost, we are also unsure if the are equal, like is a 5 DOT FOLLOWER equal to a 5 DOT CREATURE? Much less a GUIDE.<br /> <br /> I have a 4 or 5 DOT Creature (Still tweaking) which GM is fine with but we are very lost with what is appropriate for this level of background (Same for Followers), can anyone assist? For example a 5 DOT CREATURE suggests a Basilisk or other UNIQUE Legendary monsters but only provides two examples (A Basilisk and a Thunder Bird?) are there rules to create your own creature some where? How much is too powerful or too weak? Same question for FOLLOWERS really. Alright than lets start with that and than move onto other questions if you all do not mind <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (Like is there any ERRATA? as some of the Boons seem useless and some seem extremely powerful, in the same range of cost).<br /> <br /> Thanks for any help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1906-sobekh","user":"Sobekh","date":". 01-04-2014, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1906-sobekh","name":"Sobekh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T09:50:48-08:00","id":42330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sobekh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/42302-new-player-new-gm-help-with-scion#post42302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone, I am new to the Scion game. I will be both playing a game and also running one (with different groups). The GM that I am playing with is also brand new to the Scion game, we are both seeking some assistance with the game and would appreciate any help. The first question/conundrum we have is concerning RELICS and CREATURES, FOLLOWERS, GUIDES. For CREATURES, FOLLOWERS, GUIDES we are a little lost on how to actually &quot;create&quot; the stat block for these things, there not too many examples and the examples even seem to vary a bit at the same DOT cost, we are also unsure if the are equal, like is a 5 DOT FOLLOWER equal to a 5 DOT CREATURE? Much less a GUIDE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth is those guidelines were never used really. I would make them roughly equal in its uses, example: the usefulness of 10 Mortals (Followers 1) = the usefulness of a mastiff (Creature 1) = the usefulness of a wise man (Guide 1).<br /> <br /> In this example, the guide is able to provide knowledge and advices that any of the 10 mortals aren't. It would take the 10 mortals to defeat the mastiff (some just hide or run away, some are really bad at shooting and stabbing....).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sobekh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/42302-new-player-new-gm-help-with-scion#post42302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a 4 or 5 DOT Creature (Still tweaking) which GM is fine with but we are very lost with what is appropriate for this level of background (Same for Followers), can anyone assist? For example a 5 DOT CREATURE suggests a Basilisk or other UNIQUE Legendary monsters but only provides two examples (A Basilisk and a Thunder Bird?) are there rules to create your own creature some where? How much is too powerful or too weak? Same question for FOLLOWERS really. Alright than lets start with that and than move onto other questions if you all do not mind <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (Like is there any ERRATA? as some of the Boons seem useless and some seem extremely powerful, in the same range of cost).</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe there was something available on the wiki, but that is gone now, so I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> Boons and Knacks are all powerful in their own fields, although some fields come up more often then others. Also remember that the Boons and Knacks presented are just examples, if you like a Boon from another Purview that you can re-skin it in order to fit with a Purview you chose to follow, ask the ST if he would allow that re-skin (I believe it doesn't affect the game at all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T09:54:47-08:00","id":42333,"title":"","content":"Personally, for the non-Relic birthrights, I like to fold them all into the <a href=\"http://www.thecbg.org/wiki/index.php?title=Birthrights_(Modern_Mythos)\" target=\"_blank\">Retainer</a> rules over at Modern Mythos. They're quick and elegant, though they may need a bit of fudging around depending on what specifically you're making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/93-xegek","name":"Xegek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar93_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}